+"""Research candidate: exact sparse-wide refill fallback plus frozen production kernels.
+
+Adds a third GPU-predicated sparse-wide step to attn_auto for q>=6144, H100,
+FP8 KV, D128, GQA8, one KV head. Compact union remains the frozen production
+kernel. Sparse-wide visits set bitmap bits in ascending order, retains BF16
+QK/AV, and routes duplicate-bearing or >128-span tiles to selected fallback.
+All flags are recomputed on every graph replay. No production file was edited.
+
+Original module documentation follows.
+
+Env-gated mount of the tuned MiniMax-M3 block-sparse attention kernels.
+
+What this is
+------------
+The 0.24 service ran a *tuned* kernel set for MiniMax-M3 block-sparse attention
+(``tle-m3-20261019/sparse_pkg`` + the ``attn-shapes-20261019`` grid).  vLLM 0.28
+ships its own sparse-attend kernels, and it also made the packed main-KV cache
+native, so the 0.24 *packing overlay* is obsolete -- but the *tuned kernels* are
+not.  This patch mounts them onto 0.28's native layout.  Nothing is repacked and
+there is no extra copy:
+
+    kv_cache : [num_blocks, num_kv_heads, block_size, 2*head_dim]   (fp8/bf16)
+    K = kv_cache[..., :head_dim]        V = kv_cache[..., head_dim:]
+
+Kernel families (unchanged from the tuned set; only the 0.28 addressing is new):
+
+  ``attn_union_span``  one CTA per BLOCK_Q query tokens, walks the *union span*
+                       of their selected blocks with an int32 bitmap.  Best when
+                       the index is compact (deployed recent-16 / local-window
+                       index): 1.6-6.6x over the native 0.28 kernel at
+                       q >= 384, both eager and replayed.
+  ``attn_span_split``  same walk, span cut CHUNKS ways (+ weighted merge).
+  ``attn_split``       per-token walk over the *selected* blocks only, split
+                       CHUNKS ways -- exact-per-token work, so a scattered index
+                       costs nothing.  Also the decode kernel (q == 1).
+
+What is adapted to 0.28
+-----------------------
+* KV address arithmetic takes all four strides of the native 4-D packed page
+  (``stride_kv_pos = 2*head_dim``, V at ``+head_dim``) instead of the deleted
+  5-D ``_packed_view``.
+* ``topk_idx`` is the 0.28 token-major buffer ``[:num_tokens].transpose(0, 1)``;
+  every kernel takes its three strides explicitly, so the non-contiguous view is
+  read in place (no transpose copy).
+* scales come from ``layer._k_scale`` / ``layer._v_scale`` (unit by default),
+  matching the native impl; ``fp8`` QK is the tuned decode default.
+* CUDA-graph safety: no ``.item()`` or host sync. Split partials and auto flags
+  come from cached workspaces after warmup. The native ``_run_attention``
+  groups indexer + attend into one eager break in breakable modes; FULL mode
+  can capture it. Auto recomputes its device predicates in either mode.
+
+Environment gate (default OFF -- byte-identical to stock 0.28)
+-------------------------------------------------------------
+  ``M31_ATTN_TUNED``
+      unset / ``0`` / ``off``    -> not installed at all (no kernel import)
+      ``1`` / ``decode``         -> tuned decode only
+      ``2`` / ``all``            -> tuned decode + tuned prefill
+      ``prefill``                -> tuned prefill only
+  ``M31_ATTN_TUNED_PREFILL_ARM``   ``auto`` (default) | ``union`` | ``split`` |
+      ``tok`` | ``native``. ``auto`` checks each tile's selected span on the
+      GPU, runs union only for dense spans (<=32 small-q / <=64 large-q),
+      and otherwise visits only
+      selected blocks. The predicate is recomputed on every graph replay.
+      Explicit union/split arms require a compact index; they do not adapt.
+      Auto is limited to verified NVIDIA H100/SM90 devices; other devices and
+      unsupported tensor/scale configurations keep the native prefill path.
+  ``M31_ATTN_TUNED_DECODE_MIN_B``  force the tuned decode from this batch up
+      (measurement aid; default: the measured crossover at 17).
+  ``M31_ATTN_TUNED_DECODE_CHUNKS`` force the split factor (measurement aid).
+  ``M31_ATTN_TUNED_SPEC_BF16_QK`` exactly ``1`` opts multi-token decode
+      (decode_query_len > 1) into BF16 QK. The FP8 cache and split count stay
+      unchanged; q_len=1 and the default policy keep their existing math.
+
+Evidence: ``m31-028/attn-port/REPORT.md`` (parity + per-bucket tables).
